cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Quantum Local Packing: Exact Solutions via the Resultant Method"
authors:
  - family-names: Santos
    given-names: Euzebio
    alias: ebiossanto
year: 2026
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ebiossanto/IA-Research-Quantum-Local-Packing"
abstract: >-
  General algebraic framework for computing exact optimal values of the
  quantum local packing problem on arbitrary graphs and dimensions.
  Proves that c_opt(G,d) is a root of an explicit polynomial P_G(c),
  computable via the resultant method applied to Gram matrix rank constraints.
  Verified for K4/R2, K5-{04}/R3, K5/R2, C4/R2, P4/R2.
keywords:
  - quantum packing
  - local packing problem
  - Gram matrix
  - resultant method
  - algebraic optimization
  - semidefinite programming
  - Lovász theta
  - contextuality
